{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Muddy Wolf at Red Rocks feels like a natural next choice because live, electric blues connects with what draws me to Eric Clapton and Jimi Hendrix.",
    "Dig In Deep and the classic rock choices fit parts of my taste, while Traveller and Django and Jimmie connect with my interest in roots-oriented music."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "25 misses my current mood because I want blues and roots rock rather than pop.",
    "Gary Puckett's oldies collection and James Taylor's gentler songwriting do less for me today than electric blues; familiarity alone does not make them my next choice.",
    "I cannot tell whether 2 suits my interests from the title alone, so I would not commit to trying it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to lean too heavily on familiar older music, when the blues feeling and electric playing matter more to me than the era.",
    "Recognizing a classic artist does not mean I want a greatest-hits collection or deluxe reissue right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Clapton and Hendrix points toward expressive electric playing, which makes the live blues option especially appealing today.",
    "Several albums fit my broader taste, but I rarely choose more than one; a plausible match needs a stronger connection to my current mood to prompt me to act."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in classic and roots music, but only some capture the electric blues mood that makes me want to choose an album today."
}"}
